 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a><a id="req-vet-004"></a>
 
 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+The directory can be narrowed to a single specialty through an optional filter carried in the page's address. When a specialty is named, the directory lists only the veterinarians holding it, still a page at a time, and paging moves within that narrowed list `[REQ-VET-003]`. The same veterinarian list is also published in a machine-readable form as a supported surface, and it accepts the same optional specialty filter, returning only the veterinarians holding the named specialty `[REQ-VET-004]`. For both surfaces the filter matches the whole specialty name and ignores letter case, an empty or blank filter is treated as no filter at all, a specialty no veterinarian holds yields an ordinary, successful, empty result rather than a failure, and without the filter each surface behaves as it does today. Neither surface gains a form, menu, or other on-page control in this scope: the filter is expressed through the address alone, and the directory's paging links carry the named specialty so a narrowed listing stays navigable.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty named in the directory's address, when the page is opened, then only veterinarians holding that specialty are listed, a page at a time, and paging stays within the narrowed list.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty named in a letter case unlike the stored name, when the page is opened, then it matches; given a name that is only part of a specialty, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or blank specialty, when the page is opened, then it behaves as though no filter were named, and given no filter at all, then the directory is unchanged from today.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the page is opened, then an ordinary page carrying an empty list is shown.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty named in the machine-readable list's address, when it is requested, then only veterinarians holding that specialty are returned, matching the whole name and ignoring letter case.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given an empty or blank specialty, when the list is requested, then it behaves as though no filter were named, and given no filter at all, then the full list is returned as today.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the list is requested, then a successful, empty list is returned rather than a failure.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. The machine-readable list is a supported surface again under `REQ-VET-004`; the withdrawn `REQ-VET-002` stays withdrawn and its id is not reused — see the Superseded list.
 
-**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
